course: dictionary
lesson: 1356
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Candlestick is one of them. «He carries a flat candlestick» means a holder for a candle, not a stick made of candles.
explain: Look for clues. In a bedtime story or a church, a candlestick is something you hold or stand, with a candle on top. If the text is about money or prices, the same word means something quite different.
explain: Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A candle holder fits a sentence about going to bed. A bar on a price chart would not make sense there.
fact: A candlestick is a holder for a candle, with a hole or spike on top.
fact: In money and stock charts, a candlestick chart shows prices going up and down, with bars that look like candles.
fact: In the nursery rhyme, «Jack be nimble, Jack be quick, Jack jump over the candlestick.»
fact: In the board game Cluedo, the candlestick is one of the weapons.
fact: Words with more than one meaning are easier to understand when you read the words around them.
exercise: «He wears a long dressing-gown, carries a flat candlestick, and had probably been on his way to bed.» What is the candlestick in this sentence? | *A holder for a candle | A bar on a price chart | A type of long dressing-gown | A bedroom window
exercise: In the nursery rhyme, Jack jumps over the candlestick. What is a candlestick here? | A bedroom door | A long chain of price bars | A kind of stick for hitting a ball | *A candle holder
exercise: A money chart has bars that look like candles going up and down. What does candlestick mean here? | A walking stick | A holder for a candle | *A money chart showing prices going up and down | A type of candle that burns fast
test: In the board game Cluedo, what is the candlestick? | A place on the board | A player's name | *One of the weapons | A type of dice
test: In a church, what are tall candlesticks? | A bell tower | Chairs for the choir | Long shelves for books | *Holders for candles, standing on the altar
exam: In «The chart showed a candlestick that rose sharply», what does candlestick mean? | A stick for walking | A candle holder with a spike on top | *A bar on a money chart showing prices | A belt for a dressing-gown
